# SC-11 allowlist — pre-existing files with known violations.
# Each line is a repo-relative path. Lines starting with `#` are comments.
#
# These files contain pre-existing violations (English copy like "CTR" /
# "CPA" / percentages in user-facing strings). They predate the SC-11
# guard and are tracked for cleanup in a separate batch (NOT in scope of
# the Phase 14 batch 01 audit fixes).
#
# Phase 14 batch 01 audit fixes do NOT add new violations. FunnelSettingsForm,
# SC-11 guard, cpaEconomics.ts, campaignObjective.ts, and the Phase 14
# callables all pass the SC-11 scan with zero hits. The guard's zone-aware
# extractor skips lines inside className, style, and SVG attributes
# (e.g. `width="100%"`) and inside `//` / `/* */` comments so legitimate
# CSS / comment examples don't trigger false positives.
#
# Allowlist format: one path per line (no glob — exact paths only). The
# allowed paths are matched against the value returned by `path.relative`
# between the repository root and each scanned file. The guard normalizes
# both sides to forward slashes (`/`) before comparison, so this file
# uses forward slashes and works identically on Windows and POSIX runners.

